# Compiled Python bytecode is build cruft here, never a fixture. `COPY . /tests`
# would bake it into the verifier image and move the tests/ content hash that
# tags that image.
#
# Patterns are given in both forms. Docker's ignore matching does not cross
# `/`, so a bare `__pycache__` or `*.pyc` covers only the context root and
# misses nested directories.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
